  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Feel Like A Stranger** (1 review): Reviewer found it jammy, which helped while a gate problem held up their entry [7]\n- **Cumberland Blues** (1 review): Reviewer felt the slow tempo of Cumberland Blues did not suit it [7]\n- **Dark Star** (1 review): Reviewer notes Dark Star is played often lately; here it moves through Scarlet and China Doll before returning [6]\n- **Eyes of the World** (1 review): Reviewer describes Eyes of the World after the Dark Star return as powerful and bouncy [6]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **It Must've Been The Roses**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **DeadCo2019-06-07.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 18 songs; 174 min; rated 3.83/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer praises the recording's clear, detailed high end; Reviewer calls the recording's quality outstanding; Reviewer describes the recording's sound as great [2][4][5]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer's first trip to Washington; says the views on the first night were exceptional [7]\n- Reviewer mentions the Gorge recordings and asks about taping of Shoreline and Hollywood Bowl shows [3]\n- Taped from Section 102, Row 18 [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **DeadCo2019-06-07.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps CMC64V's>Schoeps VMS5u>Sound Devices 744t [1]. Also: Edited in Soundforge Pro 11, split in CDWAV, converted to FLAC with Trader's Little Helper, tagged in Foobar2000 [1]",
